{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nAfter family cutovers, reachable generic retry, `_best_effort` swallowing, duck-typed dispatch, or duplicate SDK/adapter retry would preserve the original failure class and invite future bypass.\n\n## Outcome\nProve every supported Cloud/DC mutation has exactly one typed coordinator/adapter owner, remove obsolete production fallbacks, and fail unsupported live actions before any effect.\n\n## Plan\n1. Build a dispatch census over every `MutationDirection`/`MutationAction` and Cloud/DC provider route. Require one typed owner or an intentional provider-neutral pre-effect unsupported result.\n2. Remove generic whole-operation retry, `_best_effort` write swallowing, production class-name/duck fallbacks, and duplicate SDK/adapter retry owners after their route is covered.\n3. Keep compatibility only at serialized/public read boundaries; tests use explicit protocol fakes.\n4. Add static/string and runtime poison tests that fail when removed helpers remain reachable from production.\n5. Preserve rollback as code/routing reversion plus remote re-observation; never compensate by deleting successful Jira work.\n\n## Testing\nThe census must fail on missing, duplicate, or fallback owners. Effect spies prove unsupported actions fail before local/remote writes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Every supported Cloud/DC mutation route has exactly one typed coordinator/adapter owner.\n- [x] Unsupported production actions return a typed provider-neutral error before any effect.\n- [x] Generic whole-operation retry and `_best_effort` write swallowing are unreachable from production.\n- [x] Production class-name/duck dispatch and duplicate SDK/adapter retry owners are unreachable.\n- [x] Tests use explicit declared protocols rather than production fallback paths.\n- [x] Rollback guidance requires re-observation and never remote deletion.\n\n## Out of scope\nFinal output contracts, state advancement, end-to-end validation, and docs."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787736602123631001,"uuid":"2ffc6801-b7ff-4284-afa9-ff20b3760134"}